# Dogfood components in scaffolding

When a `@standard-ui/react` component ships (or gains a variant), **update the docs site chrome** to use it instead of raw HTML / one-off Tailwind.

## Prefer package components for

| Need | Use |
|---|---|
| Text field / search | `Input` (`variant="ghost"` for quiet chrome) |
| Actions / icon buttons | `Button` (`variant`, `iconOnly`, `rounded`) |
| Labels / chips | `Badge` |
| Toggles | `Switch`, `Checkbox`, `Toggle` |
| Overlays | `Dialog`, `Popover`, `Tooltip`, etc. |

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — hand-rolled search in the shell
<input className="h-9 w-full rounded-lg border ..." />

// ✅ GOOD — design-system Input
<Input variant="ghost" type="search" className="pl-9 pr-16" />
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<button type="button" className="flex size-9 ..." />

// ✅ GOOD
<Button type="button" variant="ghost" iconOnly rounded aria-label="…" />
```

## Scope

- Shell: `components/top-bar.tsx`, `theme-toggle.tsx`, sidebar chrome when applicable
- Docs demos may still compose primitives, but shell UI should dogfood the library
- Keep accessibility (`aria-label`, focus rings) when swapping
- Layout wrappers (`div`/`aside`) stay as layout — only replace control markup
